1
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:20,251
A Ferell woman?

2
00:00:20,251 --> 00:00:22,766
Yes, Sir. There's a Ferell woman in GU.

3
00:00:22,767 --> 00:00:24,535
Are you sure?

4
00:00:25,403 --> 00:00:28,706
As far as I know,
Garpidio doesn't have a granddaughter.

5
00:00:28,706 --> 00:00:31,642
Well, those boys claim that she's a Ferell.

6
00:00:31,642 --> 00:00:33,110
Can we talk?

7
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:36,347
I want to check on you and Camille.

8
00:00:36,347 --> 00:00:38,319
She got suspended.
That's why the last time I heard,

9
00:00:38,319 --> 00:00:39,684
her father was fuming mad.

10
00:00:39,684 --> 00:00:41,519
What is this, Aira?

11
00:00:41,519 --> 00:00:43,454
Is this a trap?

12
00:00:43,454 --> 00:00:46,657
Did you make me come here
so she can laugh at me?

13
00:00:46,657 --> 00:00:47,714
This is us showing you

14
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:51,328
that we understand
what you're going through now.

15
00:00:52,129 --> 00:00:56,267
We want to assure you
that whatever you're going through,

16
00:00:56,267 --> 00:00:58,336
we are here for you.

17
00:00:58,336 --> 00:01:00,371
And if you need help,

18
00:01:00,371 --> 00:01:02,773
we're ready to help you, whatever that is.

19
00:01:02,773 --> 00:01:04,508
Still alive, Don Rogelio?

20
00:01:04,508 --> 00:01:07,445
I should ask you that question.

21
00:01:07,445 --> 00:01:10,314
Bad weeds take a long time to die.

22
00:01:10,314 --> 00:01:11,983
So, what's with this call?

23
00:01:11,983 --> 00:01:14,218
Is the world ending?

24
00:01:14,218 --> 00:01:16,954
No, not yet.

25
00:01:17,822 --> 00:01:20,491
But one of my men, George,

26
00:01:20,491 --> 00:01:24,362
had an unfortunate encounter
with your grandchildren.

27
00:01:24,362 --> 00:01:27,431
I think that's your superpower, Florence.

28
00:01:27,431 --> 00:01:31,602
Everybody eventually wants
to be friends with you.

29
00:01:31,602 --> 00:01:35,639
Even Antonia, who is the former ex
of your boyfriend, Nero.

30
00:01:35,639 --> 00:01:38,709
I want to change my life.

31
00:01:39,477 --> 00:01:43,948
I don't want to say bad things
about others...

32
00:01:43,948 --> 00:01:45,582
but...

33
00:01:46,417 --> 00:01:48,819
Florence deserves to know.

34
00:01:48,819 --> 00:01:53,957
It's not
that I want to badmouth others but...

35
00:01:54,658 --> 00:01:57,428
be careful of Antonia.

36
00:01:57,428 --> 00:01:59,397
Why?

37
00:01:59,397 --> 00:02:02,500
Well, she's the real deal, Florence.

38
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:06,170
I mean, I admit that I'm not a good girl...

39
00:02:08,421 --> 00:02:15,212
but Antonia seems like
she's hiding a different persona...

40
00:02:15,212 --> 00:02:17,782
and that's scarier.

41
00:02:17,782 --> 00:02:22,887
Excuse me, Don Ferell,
Florence is here already.

42
00:02:22,887 --> 00:02:23,921
Grandfather Garp?

43
00:02:23,921 --> 00:02:26,890
So you're Florence Dela Cruz?

44
00:03:18,404 --> 00:03:21,779
Florence,
I'd like you to meet George Villarico.

45
00:03:21,779 --> 00:03:26,820
He's an associate of Don Rogelio Almero

46
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:27,700
and this dashing gentleman here...

47
00:03:27,701 --> 00:03:30,890
I am Rogelio Almero.

48
00:03:34,291 --> 00:03:38,795
This guy, George,
claims that you attacked him.

49
00:03:39,426 --> 00:03:41,093
Is it true?

50
00:03:42,833 --> 00:03:45,870
Yes, Grandfather Garp, that's true.

51
00:03:45,870 --> 00:03:47,204
So it's true.

52
00:03:47,204 --> 00:03:50,374
I kicked him on his...

53
00:03:50,374 --> 00:03:53,043
Beep... Beep, beep...

54
00:03:54,745 --> 00:03:57,214
First, why did you meddle?

55
00:03:57,214 --> 00:04:00,251
He was talking with his daughter.

56
00:04:00,251 --> 00:04:02,586
And then when he asked you
to leave him alone,

57
00:04:02,586 --> 00:04:05,489
you kicked him there.

58
00:04:05,489 --> 00:04:07,825
Very disrespectful, Florence.

59
00:04:07,825 --> 00:04:12,162
I cannot tolerate such behavior... Cannot be.

60
00:04:17,072 --> 00:04:24,308
I'm sorry if... I kicked you on the... beep.

61
00:04:24,308 --> 00:04:26,410
But Grandfather Garp,

62
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:30,548
if I need to do it again, I'll do it.

63
00:04:30,548 --> 00:04:33,017
What? You'll do it again?

64
00:04:33,017 --> 00:04:34,218
Why?

65
00:04:34,218 --> 00:04:37,755
Because he was physically
hurting his daughter.

66
00:04:37,755 --> 00:04:42,193
What reached you was fake news,
that I just hurt him without a valid reason.

67
00:04:42,193 --> 00:04:44,395
I was defending Camille,

68
00:04:44,395 --> 00:04:47,798
and that's what my mother and father
taught me, Grandfather Garp.

69
00:04:47,798 --> 00:04:51,101
If I see someone getting abused, I must help.

70
00:04:51,101 --> 00:04:53,103
George, is this true?

71
00:04:54,305 --> 00:04:56,040
Pardon me for what I did, Sir.

72
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,675
Please let me explain.

73
00:04:57,675 --> 00:04:59,095
I'm under a lot of pressure

74
00:04:59,095 --> 00:05:02,446
and when I found out
that Camille has a problem in school,

75
00:05:02,446 --> 00:05:04,915
I completely lost my temper.

76
00:05:04,915 --> 00:05:06,850
Let's talk later.

77
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,729
What you did is admirable, Miss.

78
00:05:14,858 --> 00:05:18,728
I commend your courage
for standing up for others.

79
00:05:22,166 --> 00:05:25,236
So we've settled everything then, Almero.

80
00:05:25,236 --> 00:05:26,737
And...

81
00:05:26,737 --> 00:05:29,573
the both of you don't have
any more business here?

82
00:05:29,573 --> 00:05:33,543
So I suggest you just go.

83
00:05:35,012 --> 00:05:41,552
I think I also owe Garpidio an apology.

84
00:05:41,552 --> 00:05:44,454
I'm sorry to have wasted your time.

85
00:05:51,762 --> 00:05:53,530
Florence...

86
00:06:10,781 --> 00:06:14,385
Is it true
that you kicked him there directly?

87
00:06:14,385 --> 00:06:15,738
Yes.

88
00:06:18,589 --> 00:06:19,990
Beep.

89
00:06:19,990 --> 00:06:21,605
Good girl.

90
00:06:32,076 --> 00:06:33,971
You humiliated me in front of Garpidio.

91
00:06:33,971 --> 00:06:36,807
But, Sir, she meddled with
my conversation with Camille.

92
00:06:36,807 --> 00:06:39,075
You've hurt your own daughter!

93
00:06:39,777 --> 00:06:42,346
We are given children to love,

94
00:06:42,346 --> 00:06:47,584
to take care of, protect, and not hurt them.

95
00:06:47,584 --> 00:06:50,521
If you lay your hands on your daughter again,

96
00:06:50,521 --> 00:06:52,623
I'm going to destroy you.

97
00:06:52,623 --> 00:06:54,624
Now, get out of my face.

98
00:07:12,376 --> 00:07:13,748
Dad?

99
00:07:14,545 --> 00:07:17,750
Son... remember I told you
that I saw this girl

100
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:20,784
who could possibly be your missing daughter?

101
00:07:20,784 --> 00:07:22,853
Yes, what about it?

102
00:07:22,853 --> 00:07:25,756
I saw her again and up close this time.

103
00:07:25,756 --> 00:07:29,593
And I could feel that she's Celestina,
my missing granddaughter.

104
00:07:29,593 --> 00:07:34,264
Son... I think I found your daughter.

105
00:07:34,264 --> 00:07:36,567
I found Celestina.

106
00:07:36,567 --> 00:07:38,027
What?

107
00:07:39,370 --> 00:07:40,910
Let's go.

108
00:07:43,269 --> 00:07:45,704
You guys think Florence will be okay?

109
00:07:46,377 --> 00:07:47,478
Grandfather Garp looked kind of mad

110
00:07:47,478 --> 00:07:49,813
when he found out what happened earlier.

111
00:07:51,348 --> 00:07:52,783
This is your fault, Troy.

112
00:07:52,783 --> 00:07:54,718
You dropped grandfather's name.

113
00:07:54,718 --> 00:07:57,221
That was my way to avoid further violence.

114
00:07:57,221 --> 00:08:01,225
And how would I know
that Mr. Villarico is a staff of Don Rogelio?

115
00:08:01,225 --> 00:08:04,128
And why are you all pointing the blame at me?

116
00:08:04,128 --> 00:08:06,429
All of you played along too.

117
00:08:10,634 --> 00:08:12,802
What's up, boys?

118
00:08:13,670 --> 00:08:15,139
Nothing, Grandfather.

119
00:08:15,139 --> 00:08:17,274
We're just discussing the Grand GU Ball.

120
00:08:17,274 --> 00:08:19,777
- Yes, Grandfather.
- This year will be different.

121
00:08:19,777 --> 00:08:22,413
Yes, Grandfather,
it's going to be attractive.

122
00:08:22,413 --> 00:08:24,848
Do you believe them?

123
00:08:24,848 --> 00:08:26,216
No.

124
00:08:26,216 --> 00:08:30,810
Because when we arrived,
they became suddenly quiet and nervous.

125
00:08:30,810 --> 00:08:34,578
Marites said
that whenever they are talking about you,

126
00:08:34,578 --> 00:08:39,430
they'll suddenly become quiet
once you arrive.

127
00:08:39,430 --> 00:08:41,820
Who is Marites?

128
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:45,068
Marites is the term for gossip-mongers.

129
00:08:45,068 --> 00:08:47,805
It came from "Mare, anong latest"?

130
00:08:47,805 --> 00:08:50,240
And then it evolved to "Mare, latest"?

131
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:52,943
And now, it's Marites.

132
00:08:52,943 --> 00:08:55,779
Oh. Well, people nowadays.

133
00:08:55,779 --> 00:08:58,549
At least it settles that.

134
00:08:58,549 --> 00:09:01,284
How about your issue
with Don Rogelio, Grandfather?

135
00:09:02,352 --> 00:09:04,688
Rogelio and I is a...

136
00:09:04,688 --> 00:09:08,058
Our relationship is what you call...

137
00:09:08,058 --> 00:09:10,427
You kids call nowadays...

138
00:09:10,427 --> 00:09:12,162
"frenemies".

139
00:09:12,162 --> 00:09:14,731
Why don't you guys solve your squabbles,
Grandfather?

140
00:09:14,731 --> 00:09:15,996
You're already old

141
00:09:15,996 --> 00:09:18,402
and you guys are still competing
with your business ventures.

142
00:09:18,402 --> 00:09:20,003
That's right, Grandfather.

143
00:09:20,971 --> 00:09:25,042
The status of your relationship
seems complicated,

144
00:09:25,042 --> 00:09:28,278
but you still have collaboration projects,
right?

145
00:09:29,246 --> 00:09:34,727
The on-and-off battle between me and Rogelio
goes a long way back,

146
00:09:34,727 --> 00:09:38,489
and it's not just about politics.

147
00:09:38,489 --> 00:09:42,992
Don't tell me, Grandfather,
you even had a competition about love?

148
00:09:44,761 --> 00:09:46,463
Yes.

149
00:09:48,365 --> 00:09:51,401
Rogelio and I are best friends.

150
00:09:51,401 --> 00:09:55,138
I was even the bridge
when he was courting your grandmother.

151
00:09:55,138 --> 00:09:58,275
But your grandmother and I became closer.

152
00:09:58,275 --> 00:10:02,513
To make the story short, we became a couple.

153
00:10:02,513 --> 00:10:03,981
You're our idol, Grandfather.

154
00:10:03,981 --> 00:10:06,650
You're really something else,
Grandfather Garp.

155
00:10:06,650 --> 00:10:10,720
This is the first time we learned
that Don Rogelio liked Grandmother.

156
00:10:11,922 --> 00:10:15,459
And that's how we became frenemies.

157
00:10:15,459 --> 00:10:17,761
To be honest,

158
00:10:17,761 --> 00:10:20,097
before Rogelio even set eyes
on your grandmother,

159
00:10:20,097 --> 00:10:22,799
I've already fallen in love with her.

160
00:10:22,799 --> 00:10:26,870
But Rogelio and I were best of friends,
so I stepped aside.

161
00:10:28,205 --> 00:10:32,408
But what can I do,
your grandmother really loves me.

162
00:10:33,176 --> 00:10:36,046
That's right. Of course,
that's Grandfather Garp...

163
00:10:36,046 --> 00:10:40,417
Charming, kind, and sweet.

164
00:10:40,417 --> 00:10:43,287
Of course, she'll choose you.

165
00:10:43,287 --> 00:10:45,054
Deserve!

166
00:10:47,224 --> 00:10:51,028
Unfortunately, my friendship with Rogelio
was ruined.

167
00:10:51,028 --> 00:10:54,164
From then on, he resented me.

168
00:10:54,898 --> 00:10:58,835
We continued our partnership
in our businesses but...

169
00:10:58,835 --> 00:11:01,471
things have never been the same.

170
00:11:03,407 --> 00:11:07,878
All your grandmother's efforts
for Rogelio and I to patch things up

171
00:11:07,878 --> 00:11:10,981
didn't work, because we always fight.

172
00:11:10,981 --> 00:11:14,384
And that affected our business decisions.

173
00:11:14,384 --> 00:11:18,789
We lost so many transactions
because we can't get along,

174
00:11:18,789 --> 00:11:20,857
even with the smallest details,

175
00:11:20,857 --> 00:11:25,428
until our partnership got dissolved.

176
00:11:28,131 --> 00:11:31,568
To be honest, I miss my best friend.

177
00:11:31,568 --> 00:11:35,175
Rogelio and I are like brothers.

178
00:11:35,175 --> 00:11:36,905
Not that I'm blaming Amanda,

179
00:11:36,905 --> 00:11:40,543
but I hope from the start,
we were able to talk about it.

180
00:11:41,211 --> 00:11:43,516
Because now...

181
00:11:43,516 --> 00:11:45,568
Rogelio feels that I betrayed him

182
00:11:45,568 --> 00:11:48,485
because I didn't tell him right away

183
00:11:48,485 --> 00:11:52,135
that I have feelings for Amanda too.

184
00:12:00,729 --> 00:12:02,099
Guys, help me.

185
00:12:02,099 --> 00:12:04,001
I'm chatting with this chick.

186
00:12:04,001 --> 00:12:05,636
You know, I'm not used to chatting.

187
00:12:05,636 --> 00:12:07,304
I'm a skilled face-to-face talker.

188
00:12:07,304 --> 00:12:10,607
What's the difference between chatting online
and chatting in person?

189
00:12:10,607 --> 00:12:11,875
That's right.

190
00:12:11,875 --> 00:12:13,710
In case you forget, Aldus,

191
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:15,912
Troy has a typographical error problem.

192
00:12:15,912 --> 00:12:18,015
Remember when he was texting his crush,

193
00:12:18,015 --> 00:12:20,550
instead of texting,
"I want to tuck you up in bed",

194
00:12:20,550 --> 00:12:22,419
he texted "I want to F you up in bed".

195
00:12:22,419 --> 00:12:24,186
What's with you?

196
00:12:24,186 --> 00:12:26,423
- That was good.
- What will I tell her?

197
00:12:26,423 --> 00:12:28,859
Basic... Ask first what she looks like.

198
00:12:28,859 --> 00:12:30,927
Or better, ask her to send her picture.

199
00:12:30,927 --> 00:12:32,528
There.

200
00:12:33,264 --> 00:12:35,565
Baby girl, send me your picture.

201
00:12:35,565 --> 00:12:37,167
Baby girl?

202
00:12:37,167 --> 00:12:42,072
So, beauty is just your qualifications
to talk to someone?

203
00:12:42,072 --> 00:12:44,964
You'd lose interest
if you are talking to an ugly person.

204
00:12:44,964 --> 00:12:46,677
- Exactly.
- What?

205
00:12:46,677 --> 00:12:48,712
Wouldn't you lose your interest more

206
00:12:48,712 --> 00:12:50,681
if you're talking to someone who's...

207
00:12:50,681 --> 00:12:52,149
whom Taylor Swift would be ashamed of,

208
00:12:52,149 --> 00:12:53,850
but you'll also be embarrassed

209
00:12:53,850 --> 00:12:57,187
with the five-year-old capacity of her brain?

210
00:12:57,187 --> 00:12:58,758
And what if she gets turned off

211
00:12:58,758 --> 00:13:02,062
because you asked her
to send a picture so soon,

212
00:13:02,062 --> 00:13:04,101
and it just so happened that she's beautiful

213
00:13:04,101 --> 00:13:07,130
like a goddess, intelligent, honor student?

214
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:08,598
You'll quickly lose the chance

215
00:13:08,598 --> 00:13:10,867
to have a potential beauty-and-brains friend,

216
00:13:10,867 --> 00:13:13,336
or even a girlfriend.

217
00:13:15,572 --> 00:13:17,941
Florence has a point.

218
00:13:17,941 --> 00:13:20,210
Okay, since you all know too much,

219
00:13:20,210 --> 00:13:22,846
why don't you do this, since you're good?

220
00:13:22,846 --> 00:13:24,815
- Do the honors.
- Stay here.

221
00:13:24,815 --> 00:13:26,449
Move.

222
00:13:27,384 --> 00:13:29,018
Hold this.

223
00:13:33,824 --> 00:13:35,458
Let's see what you can do.

224
00:13:49,701 --> 00:13:52,399
[alvis_jester: What's your favorite novel?]

225
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:55,234
[ninjacopygirl1409: Little Lord Fauntleroy.
My teacher asked me to read it before,]

226
00:13:55,234 --> 00:13:58,067
[and I fell in love with the main character.]

227
00:13:58,348 --> 00:14:00,417
This girl will like you.

228
00:14:00,417 --> 00:14:03,854
She is fond of boys who are mama's boy.

229
00:14:03,854 --> 00:14:07,057
Just like Cedric Errol,
the main character in her favorite novel.

230
00:14:07,057 --> 00:14:09,126
Just like you, a mama's boy.

231
00:14:09,126 --> 00:14:11,094
Mama's boy? Of course not.

232
00:14:11,094 --> 00:14:13,008
No? What do you mean you're not?

233
00:14:13,008 --> 00:14:16,233
I hear you every day calling your mom.

234
00:14:16,233 --> 00:14:17,501
"Good night, Mama."

235
00:14:17,501 --> 00:14:18,769
"Good morning, Mama."

236
00:14:18,769 --> 00:14:19,970
"I love you, Mama."

237
00:14:19,970 --> 00:14:21,508
- "I miss you."
- That's so sweet.

238
00:14:21,508 --> 00:14:25,478
So you're a mama's boy in a positive light.

239
00:14:26,910 --> 00:14:29,112
See? You suddenly became meek.

240
00:14:30,847 --> 00:14:33,466
What's wrong with loving your mom?

241
00:14:33,466 --> 00:14:36,135
No, don't be ashamed of being a mama's boy.

242
00:14:44,367 --> 00:14:45,434
[alvis_jester: How many siblings
do you have?]

243
00:14:45,434 --> 00:14:47,234
[ninjacopygirl1409: Three,
and I'm the only girl and the youngest.]

244
00:15:07,434 --> 00:15:10,233
[alvis_jester: Are you a K-Pop fan?]

245
00:15:10,234 --> 00:15:12,066
[ninjacopygirl1409: I'm more
of a PPop fan, SB19, FTW,]

246
00:15:12,067 --> 00:15:13,934
[but I also love BTS and EXO.]

247
00:15:20,860 --> 00:15:22,527
Deal-breaker.

248
00:15:30,067 --> 00:15:34,399
[alvis_jester: Do you like basketball?]

249
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:37,233
[ninjacopygirl1409:
I got influenced by my brothers.]

250
00:15:37,234 --> 00:15:40,099
[I love Draymond Green.]

251
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:42,315
I like this girl.

252
00:15:47,557 --> 00:15:49,392
This girl is mine, dude.

253
00:15:51,928 --> 00:15:53,163
But...

254
00:15:53,163 --> 00:15:54,897
Florence, wait.

255
00:15:56,233 --> 00:15:59,069
Why does it seem
like you're doing an interview?

256
00:15:59,069 --> 00:16:02,138
Aren't you going to say some things about me?

257
00:16:02,138 --> 00:16:03,940
About you?

258
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:04,975
Interview?

259
00:16:04,975 --> 00:16:06,176
This is not like an interview.

260
00:16:06,176 --> 00:16:08,612
That's the problem with you.

261
00:16:08,612 --> 00:16:11,081
You're always after yourselves.

262
00:16:11,081 --> 00:16:13,083
And you want to impress,

263
00:16:13,083 --> 00:16:15,118
that's why you end up
talking about yourselves.

264
00:16:15,118 --> 00:16:16,656
"I'm handsome", "This is what I want",

265
00:16:16,656 --> 00:16:19,022
"I'm playing basketball", blah blah...

266
00:16:19,022 --> 00:16:22,092
So the people you're talking to
have lost their interest in you.

267
00:16:22,092 --> 00:16:23,593
If you want the girl,

268
00:16:23,593 --> 00:16:27,797
you have to make them feel
that you're interested in her.

269
00:16:27,797 --> 00:16:29,799
What's there not to like?

270
00:16:33,767 --> 00:16:35,467
[ninjacopygirl1409:
How about you, alvis_jester?]

271
00:16:35,467 --> 00:16:37,200
[Tell me something about you too.
What's your favorite novel?]

272
00:16:38,251 --> 00:16:40,133
There's your cue.

273
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:43,313
Now is the time you chat about yourself,

274
00:16:43,313 --> 00:16:45,748
and not at the beginning
when you are just starting.

275
00:16:46,383 --> 00:16:47,984
It's game time.

276
00:16:49,419 --> 00:16:51,153
It's crunch time, boys.

277
00:16:58,181 --> 00:16:59,839
Look. We're both gamers.

278
00:16:59,839 --> 00:17:01,503
- Yes, sir.
- What are you waiting for?

279
00:17:01,503 --> 00:17:03,270
Ask her to send a picture.

280
00:17:03,270 --> 00:17:04,467
A picture.

281
00:17:04,467 --> 00:17:05,902
- Picture.
- No, bro.

282
00:17:05,902 --> 00:17:07,704
I don't want to pressure her.

283
00:17:07,704 --> 00:17:09,805
She might get turned off by me.

284
00:17:11,423 --> 00:17:12,769
Good job, Troy.

285
00:17:12,769 --> 00:17:14,911
Fast learner, in fairness.

286
00:17:14,911 --> 00:17:19,389
But, Troy, just in case you don't like
her physical appearance,

287
00:17:19,389 --> 00:17:20,894
don't just dump her.

288
00:17:20,894 --> 00:17:22,308
That's rude.

289
00:17:22,308 --> 00:17:24,054
- Yeah.
- Of course not.

290
00:17:24,054 --> 00:17:25,889
And I like this girl.

291
00:17:25,889 --> 00:17:27,824
I want her to be my friend.

292
00:17:27,824 --> 00:17:32,629
And beauty is not a qualification
to become my friend.

293
00:17:32,629 --> 00:17:34,553
Look at yourself.

294
00:17:34,553 --> 00:17:36,599
We're friends, right?

295
00:17:38,769 --> 00:17:42,146
Are you telling me that I'm not beautiful?

296
00:17:42,146 --> 00:17:45,388
Then why do I see a queen beauty

297
00:17:45,388 --> 00:17:48,458
whenever I see my reflection?

298
00:17:49,459 --> 00:17:52,062
You're so beautiful. You're so charming.

299
00:17:52,062 --> 00:17:56,433
Why don't you ask... Nero?

300
00:17:56,433 --> 00:17:58,501
Where is he?

301
00:17:58,501 --> 00:18:00,703
Where is that fool?

302
00:18:03,133 --> 00:18:06,000
[Henry's Roasted Chicken]

303
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:11,948
Okay, let's see each other in school,
and let's do a checklist

304
00:18:11,948 --> 00:18:15,619
so we can make sure
we won't forget anything for the ball.

305
00:18:15,619 --> 00:18:17,587
Okay, bye.

306
00:18:20,757 --> 00:18:23,233
Perfect timing, it's freshly cooked.

307
00:18:23,234 --> 00:18:25,074
- Mr. Henry?
- Yes?

308
00:18:25,075 --> 00:18:29,299
I'll have the usual,
not too big but not too small.

309
00:18:29,299 --> 00:18:33,436
I'll have the medium size,
it shouldn't be too big.

310
00:18:33,436 --> 00:18:34,689
That's it.

311
00:18:35,472 --> 00:18:38,007
And don't forget my favorite sauce.

312
00:18:40,510 --> 00:18:42,646
There, the other one, Mister.

313
00:18:42,646 --> 00:18:44,247
- Florence?
- That's it.

314
00:18:47,784 --> 00:18:50,453
Don Rogelio, it's you.

315
00:18:50,453 --> 00:18:52,355
Good morning.

316
00:18:53,089 --> 00:18:58,061
Look, Florence, I'm sorry
that we met under unfortunate circumstances.

317
00:18:58,061 --> 00:19:01,564
But when I learned that there was an incident

318
00:19:01,564 --> 00:19:03,848
involving the grandsons of Don Garpidio
with one of my people,

319
00:19:03,848 --> 00:19:06,369
I had to deal with it right away.

320
00:19:06,369 --> 00:19:09,139
Garpidio and I have had a colorful history,

321
00:19:09,139 --> 00:19:12,709
that's why I need to fix it right away
before things get worse.

322
00:19:12,709 --> 00:19:17,113
I understand, there's nothing to worry about.

323
00:19:17,113 --> 00:19:19,524
But now that I know the truth,

324
00:19:19,524 --> 00:19:21,685
I have dealt with George,

325
00:19:21,685 --> 00:19:26,156
and I assure you
that he will no longer hurt Camille.

326
00:19:26,156 --> 00:19:28,691
That's great to hear.

327
00:19:30,193 --> 00:19:32,796
Oh, but look, what do we have here?

328
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:35,966
Is Mr. Henry's chicken your favorite too?

329
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:39,569
Yes, this is my favorite chicken
in the whole Levante.

330
00:19:39,569 --> 00:19:41,738
When I'm sad, that's my comfort food.

331
00:19:41,738 --> 00:19:43,031
That makes me happy.

332
00:19:43,031 --> 00:19:43,801
Just a little push

333
00:19:43,801 --> 00:19:47,209
and I'll call it
the joyful chicken of Mr. Henry.

334
00:19:48,378 --> 00:19:50,914
Is this your favorite too?

335
00:19:50,914 --> 00:19:52,438
Of course.

336
00:19:52,438 --> 00:19:53,267
Did you know

337
00:19:53,267 --> 00:19:56,148
that Mr. Henry uses mango tree wood
for roasting?

338
00:19:56,148 --> 00:19:58,221
That's why his chicken is delicious.

339
00:19:58,221 --> 00:20:00,056
Wow, that's cool.

340
00:20:00,056 --> 00:20:03,426
You also know a lot about food.

341
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:06,997
Actually, I didn't discover this place.

342
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:09,131
It was my daughter-in-law...

343
00:20:10,433 --> 00:20:12,569
Alyanna.

344
00:20:12,569 --> 00:20:15,472
Unfortunately, she's no longer here.

345
00:20:15,472 --> 00:20:18,641
That's why I pass by here to remember her.

346
00:20:19,542 --> 00:20:22,912
How wonderful a woman she was.

347
00:20:22,912 --> 00:20:24,881
That's sad.

348
00:20:24,881 --> 00:20:28,751
But it's okay. Don't worry, because...

349
00:20:30,286 --> 00:20:32,288
Can you smell that?

350
00:20:33,599 --> 00:20:36,100
- Can you smell that?
- Yes.

351
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:39,520
It smells like
freshly cooked roasted chicken of Mr. Henry.

352
00:20:40,230 --> 00:20:42,399
The scent is powerful, right?

353
00:20:42,399 --> 00:20:44,100
You can smell it right away.

354
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:47,604
That's why I'm sure
Ms. Alyanna can smell that in heaven.

355
00:20:47,604 --> 00:20:48,967
And I'm sure

356
00:20:48,968 --> 00:20:51,374
she's looking at St. Peter's chicken
with dagger looks

357
00:20:51,374 --> 00:20:53,843
because she wants to roast it.

358
00:20:55,678 --> 00:20:57,714
You are adorable, Florence.

359
00:20:57,714 --> 00:21:00,583
It's been a while
since someone made me laugh.

360
00:21:00,583 --> 00:21:03,853
I hope this is not the last time
I'll be talking to you.

361
00:21:03,853 --> 00:21:06,114
That's for sure,

362
00:21:06,114 --> 00:21:08,391
especially now that we get along
when it comes to roasted chicken.

363
00:21:08,391 --> 00:21:09,926
Of course.

364
00:21:09,926 --> 00:21:12,295
Roasted chicken buddies.

365
00:21:12,295 --> 00:21:14,563
Chicken buddies for life.

366
00:21:19,769 --> 00:21:21,304
- Let's order now.
- It's done.

367
00:21:21,304 --> 00:21:23,706
- Thank you.
- I'll pay for this.

368
00:21:23,706 --> 00:21:25,642
- Are you sure?
- Yes, add some more.

369
00:21:25,642 --> 00:21:26,910
Okay, how many?

370
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:28,086
Three more.

371
00:21:28,086 --> 00:21:29,383
- Coming right up.
- Three?

372
00:21:29,383 --> 00:21:32,382
- You'll consume all that?
- No, you'll bring that home.

373
00:21:32,382 --> 00:21:33,950
Me?

374
00:21:33,950 --> 00:21:37,087
- I'll bring it home?
- Yes.

375
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,422
I think that's good for a month.

376
00:21:41,347 --> 00:21:45,194
It was suggested to me by my friend
who owns an IT company.

377
00:21:45,194 --> 00:21:48,364
He sent me a computer graphics expert.

378
00:21:49,146 --> 00:21:50,179
I didn't believe it

379
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:52,800
when the computer graphics specialist told me

380
00:21:52,801 --> 00:21:56,729
that they can give
an approximate image of Celestina

381
00:21:56,729 --> 00:21:59,339
if she grows up into a young woman,

382
00:21:59,339 --> 00:22:01,977
by uploading her baby picture.

383
00:22:04,510 --> 00:22:05,715
Look.

384
00:22:05,715 --> 00:22:08,250
That is the rendered picture.

385
00:22:10,841 --> 00:22:13,176
That is Celestina's baby picture.

386
00:22:16,379 --> 00:22:17,534
I have a strong feeling

387
00:22:17,534 --> 00:22:22,700
that this is
your missing daughter, Celestina.

388
00:22:22,701 --> 00:22:26,102
I believe that this girl is my granddaughter.

389
00:22:37,534 --> 00:22:39,803
You had this kid followed?

390
00:22:40,907 --> 00:22:42,844
Have you gone crazy?

391
00:22:42,844 --> 00:22:46,589
Are you trying to pick a fight
with the Ferells?

392
00:22:46,589 --> 00:22:48,527
What are you talking about?

393
00:22:49,628 --> 00:22:51,163
Can you just stop using my daughter

394
00:22:51,163 --> 00:22:53,698
so you won't feel guilty about what happened?

395
00:22:54,333 --> 00:22:56,502
Do you know what this means?

396
00:22:56,502 --> 00:22:59,506
If people find out about
your obsession with my dead daughter,

397
00:22:59,506 --> 00:23:01,673
they'll think you're crazy.

398
00:23:06,111 --> 00:23:08,614
Celestina is alive!

399
00:23:08,614 --> 00:23:11,350
I can feel it in my heart.

400
00:23:11,350 --> 00:23:15,287
And if you refuse to believe that,
let me look for her.

401
00:23:16,855 --> 00:23:18,757
Don't force yourself to believe
that Celestina is still alive,

402
00:23:18,757 --> 00:23:20,192
because she's already dead.

403
00:23:20,192 --> 00:23:23,795
She and Alyanna are already dead,
and that's what I can feel.

404
00:23:24,698 --> 00:23:29,235
Do you think the hurt I feel
from what happened, has gone?

405
00:23:29,235 --> 00:23:32,798
Do you think I don't wake up every day

406
00:23:32,798 --> 00:23:35,907
feeling sorry because I failed to save them?

407
00:23:36,875 --> 00:23:40,679
There's no minute or moment
that I don't think about them.

408
00:23:42,848 --> 00:23:46,986
But even if it hurts, that's the truth.

409
00:23:46,986 --> 00:23:49,688
I choose to live for them.

410
00:23:49,688 --> 00:23:52,841
That is my way of honoring their memory.

411
00:23:52,841 --> 00:23:54,827
To live.

412
00:23:54,827 --> 00:23:57,529
And somehow try to be happy.

413
00:24:01,233 --> 00:24:03,402
Stop chasing ghosts.

414
00:24:03,402 --> 00:24:07,739
Stop chasing the past
before you get hurt or hurt someone else.

415
00:24:18,684 --> 00:24:21,186
Good morning, Gyronellans.

416
00:24:21,186 --> 00:24:26,392
And we just finished the final plans
for this year's Grand GU Ball.

417
00:24:26,392 --> 00:24:30,629
Confirmed, for the first time ever
in the university's history,

418
00:24:30,629 --> 00:24:33,198
this year's ball will be about giving back.

419
00:24:33,198 --> 00:24:37,603
A charity event with the theme,
"Return to Kindness".

420
00:24:37,603 --> 00:24:39,238
We'll still have the usual fun.

421
00:24:39,238 --> 00:24:41,206
But this time, with a cause.

422
00:24:41,206 --> 00:24:44,743
And each plate will cost about 50,000 pesos,

423
00:24:44,743 --> 00:24:49,782
and all funds raised will be given to
several chosen charitable institutions.

424
00:24:49,782 --> 00:24:52,451
<i>And this is our little way
of reminding people</i>

425
00:24:52,451 --> 00:24:55,954
<i>that we cannot just live
in our own bubble of privilege.</i>

426
00:24:55,954 --> 00:24:57,956
<i>Thank you to
the College of Communication Arts</i>

427
00:24:57,956 --> 00:25:00,826
<i>for this marvelous proposal.</i>

428
00:25:00,826 --> 00:25:03,462
<i>And a special shout out
to its representative,</i>

429
00:25:03,462 --> 00:25:05,898
<i>Ms. Florence Dela Cruz.</i>

430
00:25:05,898 --> 00:25:07,700
<i>You're something else, Florence.</i>

431
00:25:07,700 --> 00:25:12,338
<i>Your mind is not just rich,
but your heart is full too.</i>

432
00:25:12,338 --> 00:25:13,672
Facts.

433
00:25:13,672 --> 00:25:20,579
Anyways, I still have a lot of ideas
within the ball to raise funds.

434
00:25:20,579 --> 00:25:22,681
That's good, Camille, just make suggestions,

435
00:25:22,681 --> 00:25:26,418
but I'll ask a favor from you,
if that's okay.

436
00:25:26,418 --> 00:25:28,087
Anything.

437
00:25:28,087 --> 00:25:32,591
Would it be okay if you oversee some things
during the ball?

438
00:25:32,591 --> 00:25:35,427
I can handle the preparations.

439
00:25:35,427 --> 00:25:37,295
You're not coming?

440
00:25:38,764 --> 00:25:40,432
But why?

441
00:25:41,166 --> 00:25:43,769
Aren't you updated with the latest?

442
00:25:43,769 --> 00:25:45,937
You're always updated.

443
00:25:46,772 --> 00:25:50,309
I'm just a scholar here in the GU.

444
00:25:50,309 --> 00:25:54,145
I can't afford
that 50,000 pesos per plate price.

445
00:25:55,414 --> 00:25:56,415
Gosh.

446
00:25:56,415 --> 00:26:00,008
Oh, yeah, you're poor.

447
00:26:00,008 --> 00:26:01,987
Hey.

448
00:26:01,987 --> 00:26:04,189
- Oh my God. I'm sorry.
- Oh my God.

449
00:26:04,189 --> 00:26:06,525
I didn't mean to offend you.

450
00:26:06,525 --> 00:26:08,727
I just lack sleep.

451
00:26:08,727 --> 00:26:12,197
That's okay, but why did you lack sleep?

452
00:26:14,133 --> 00:26:17,770
Actually, even if you don't lack sleep,
that's the truth.

453
00:26:17,770 --> 00:26:18,837
I'm poor.

454
00:26:18,837 --> 00:26:21,540
I belong to the lower class.

455
00:26:21,540 --> 00:26:24,876
So, Camille,
you take charge during the ball, okay?

456
00:26:25,710 --> 00:26:29,081
Florence, oh, come on.

457
00:26:29,081 --> 00:26:30,582
You'll be there.

458
00:26:30,582 --> 00:26:34,520
And I'm sure Nero will ask you
to be his date.

459
00:26:34,520 --> 00:26:36,622
He'll pay for you.

460
00:26:36,622 --> 00:26:38,123
- That's true.
- Right?

461
00:26:38,123 --> 00:26:41,860
- Oh my, exciting.
- That's exciting.

462
00:26:41,860 --> 00:26:44,729
How about you? Do you have a date already?

463
00:26:45,898 --> 00:26:51,336
Well, this university does not forget easily.

464
00:26:52,204 --> 00:26:53,308
You know what?

465
00:26:53,308 --> 00:26:56,842
Aira and I have already made a mark
as being mean and bullies.

466
00:26:56,842 --> 00:26:59,945
And after what happened on Agora Day,

467
00:26:59,945 --> 00:27:03,482
we no longer expect
that someone will ask us out.

468
00:27:03,482 --> 00:27:04,817
Yeah.

469
00:27:04,817 --> 00:27:06,585
We'll be each other's date.

470
00:27:06,585 --> 00:27:08,386
Yes!

471
00:27:13,225 --> 00:27:16,228
How about you, Lina? You're smiling there.
Do you have a date already?

472
00:27:16,228 --> 00:27:17,262
None.

473
00:27:17,262 --> 00:27:20,199
Should I expect someone to ask me out

474
00:27:20,199 --> 00:27:24,870
when nobody is interested to talk me?

475
00:27:24,870 --> 00:27:26,717
- But I will still attend the ball.
- Seriously?

476
00:27:26,717 --> 00:27:29,040
With a date or none.

477
00:27:31,243 --> 00:27:33,412
No one wants to talk to you?

478
00:27:33,412 --> 00:27:36,181
No one is really interested in you?

479
00:27:36,181 --> 00:27:38,225
- But you lack sleep?
- But you lack sleep?

480
00:27:38,225 --> 00:27:39,618
You said you lack sleep last night.

481
00:27:39,618 --> 00:27:42,320
- What did you do?
- Since when did you learn to stay up late?

482
00:27:43,789 --> 00:27:48,893
Hey, Lina is keeping secrets.

483
00:27:53,732 --> 00:27:58,503
You know... I wish someone will ask me out.

484
00:27:59,928 --> 00:28:02,430
- Me too.
- Me too.

485
00:28:02,430 --> 00:28:03,573
Someone will ask you out too.

486
00:28:03,573 --> 00:28:07,079
Of course, you of all people.

487
00:28:07,079 --> 00:28:08,877
OMG!

488
00:28:08,877 --> 00:28:10,882
- What?
- Someone is coming.

489
00:28:12,010 --> 00:28:13,409
Oh my God.

490
00:28:13,409 --> 00:28:14,887
Hi, Camille.

491
00:28:14,887 --> 00:28:16,143
Hi.

492
00:28:16,143 --> 00:28:20,915
Can I invite Chelle to be my date
at the Grand GU Ball?

493
00:28:20,915 --> 00:28:23,151
It's... What?

494
00:28:23,151 --> 00:28:26,924
- Yes, it's Chelle.
- Why are you asking permission from me?

495
00:28:26,924 --> 00:28:29,067
That's because...

496
00:28:31,815 --> 00:28:34,010
Let me stop you there.

497
00:28:34,010 --> 00:28:36,375
I'm a changed person now.

498
00:28:36,375 --> 00:28:39,463
I'm no longer the old Camille.

499
00:28:39,463 --> 00:28:42,518
There's no more leader in our group.

500
00:28:42,518 --> 00:28:44,072
We're all equal.

501
00:28:44,072 --> 00:28:48,276
So... if you want to ask Chelle...

502
00:28:48,276 --> 00:28:50,111
- Chelle...
- Chelle...

503
00:28:50,111 --> 00:28:51,495
Go ask her.

504
00:28:51,495 --> 00:28:52,924
Chelle...

505
00:30:34,993 --> 00:30:36,620
Antonia.

506
00:30:36,620 --> 00:30:38,296
Thank you.

507
00:30:39,450 --> 00:30:42,152
You're so sweet, thank you.

508
00:30:45,537 --> 00:30:49,140
- Did you like it?
- Yes, thank you.

509
00:31:32,684 --> 00:31:34,452
Let's go.

510
00:31:39,038 --> 00:31:41,093
- Florence, wait.
- Florence?

511
00:31:41,093 --> 00:31:43,094
Florence, wait.

512
00:31:43,829 --> 00:31:45,831
Please, just let me be alone.

513
00:31:45,831 --> 00:31:47,489
Florence...

514
00:31:47,489 --> 00:31:48,897
Trust me.

515
00:31:48,897 --> 00:31:52,491
The last thing you want
is to be alone at this moment.

516
00:31:52,491 --> 00:31:53,733
We're here for you.

517
00:31:53,733 --> 00:31:56,708
Don't carry this by yourself.

518
00:31:58,006 --> 00:31:59,242
I just want to be alone.

519
00:31:59,242 --> 00:32:01,410
Please let me be.

520
00:32:02,675 --> 00:32:04,342
Florence...

521
00:32:05,319 --> 00:32:06,951
What happened?

522
00:32:21,901 --> 00:32:24,303
Won't you say anything?

523
00:32:26,525 --> 00:32:28,827
You're a philosopher, right?

524
00:32:31,855 --> 00:32:34,523
No, not this time.

525
00:32:37,983 --> 00:32:42,154
I need your soothing words right now.

526
00:32:42,154 --> 00:32:47,459
Your words can lighten my load.

527
00:32:47,459 --> 00:32:51,896
Words, if it comes from the heart,
can be comforting.

528
00:32:52,772 --> 00:32:56,667
But in our case right now... it won't work.

529
00:32:57,943 --> 00:33:01,612
Because it's more effective
if you cry out all your pain.

530
00:33:02,307 --> 00:33:07,735
I once read that God created us
to become the strongest.

531
00:33:07,735 --> 00:33:12,124
Because he gave us the strongest weapon
to protect us from pain.

532
00:33:12,124 --> 00:33:15,052
And that's our ability to cry.

533
00:33:16,741 --> 00:33:19,897
So just cry it all out

534
00:33:19,897 --> 00:33:23,194
and take out all the pain
you're feeling right now.

535
00:33:32,637 --> 00:33:34,840
To be fair,

536
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:40,878
you were able to say words
that made me feel better.

537
00:33:43,082 --> 00:33:44,885
It's going to be okay.

538
00:33:57,329 --> 00:33:59,164
This is nice.

539
00:33:59,164 --> 00:34:02,900
You remembered well
what's my favorite flower.

540
00:34:04,924 --> 00:34:07,158
Are you happy?

541
00:34:07,158 --> 00:34:08,806
Yes.

542
00:34:20,103 --> 00:34:21,853
That's what's important.

543
00:34:21,853 --> 00:34:23,554
That you're happy.

544
00:34:35,424 --> 00:34:37,892
I'm happy that you invited me, Sir.

545
00:34:37,892 --> 00:34:41,208
Your sizeable contribution
to our beloved university

546
00:34:41,208 --> 00:34:43,488
will certainly be a big help.

547
00:34:43,488 --> 00:34:46,992
I've always been interested
in how I could help Gyronella.

548
00:34:46,992 --> 00:34:52,097
After all, this is one of the best
universities that produce top talents.

549
00:34:52,097 --> 00:34:53,331
And all these years,

550
00:34:53,331 --> 00:34:57,102
my company benefited
from the quality of your graduates.

551
00:34:57,102 --> 00:35:00,171
Thank you, Sir,
for recognizing our hard work.

552
00:35:00,171 --> 00:35:05,377
Indeed, our graduates are
our greatest reputation, our pride.

553
00:35:05,377 --> 00:35:09,948
But if there's one reputation
that we want to erase,

554
00:35:09,948 --> 00:35:14,319
that's our reputation
as a rich kid university.

555
00:35:14,319 --> 00:35:15,854
And with your donation,

556
00:35:15,854 --> 00:35:18,331
we can expand our scholarship program

557
00:35:18,331 --> 00:35:23,828
to make the university accessible
to children from underserved communities.

558
00:35:23,828 --> 00:35:26,398
That's very noble of you, Dean.

559
00:35:26,398 --> 00:35:28,566
It's about time.

560
00:35:28,566 --> 00:35:34,572
It would be a shame if the quality
of education provided by the school

561
00:35:34,572 --> 00:35:39,277
is only exclusive to the wealthy.

562
00:35:39,277 --> 00:35:41,579
Which brings me to my point.

563
00:35:43,548 --> 00:35:46,818
I'm interested in one of your scholars.

564
00:35:46,818 --> 00:35:48,386
Scholars?

565
00:35:48,386 --> 00:35:49,921
Yes.

566
00:35:49,921 --> 00:35:53,491
Her name is Florence Dela Cruz.

567
00:35:53,491 --> 00:35:57,061
And if possible,
I would like to know everything about her.

568
00:36:14,079 --> 00:36:16,113
Is everything okay?

569
00:36:18,383 --> 00:36:19,984
Yes, Grandfather.

570
00:36:21,419 --> 00:36:23,320
Everything is okay.

571
00:36:25,557 --> 00:36:26,891
It's so quiet.

572
00:36:26,891 --> 00:36:29,727
Troy, don't you have any jokes?

573
00:36:29,727 --> 00:36:32,229
I'm still collecting some jokes.

574
00:36:35,233 --> 00:36:39,136
Is it just me
or Florence's cooking is a bit salty?

575
00:36:50,386 --> 00:36:52,221
Yes, it's salty.

576
00:36:56,160 --> 00:36:58,662
Does Florence have a problem?

577
00:37:05,597 --> 00:37:08,066
No one wants to talk.

578
00:37:08,066 --> 00:37:09,838
Okay.

579
00:37:09,838 --> 00:37:11,639
Just be sure...

580
00:37:12,504 --> 00:37:16,174
that if you mess up something, you fix it.

581
00:37:16,174 --> 00:37:18,776
You do what a Ferell should do.

582
00:37:32,924 --> 00:37:34,525
Nero?

583
00:37:36,161 --> 00:37:37,529
Nero!

584
00:37:37,529 --> 00:37:39,163
Nero!

585
00:37:39,932 --> 00:37:41,792
Are you having fun?

586
00:37:41,792 --> 00:37:43,835
What's your problem?

587
00:37:43,835 --> 00:37:45,370
Not good, Bro.

588
00:37:45,370 --> 00:37:48,173
You're disappointing, man.

589
00:37:48,173 --> 00:37:49,807
You're disappointing.

590
00:37:49,807 --> 00:37:52,840
Please, don't meddle.

591
00:37:52,840 --> 00:37:54,850
What are you talking about?

592
00:37:56,748 --> 00:37:58,917
You're scum, bro!

593
00:37:58,917 --> 00:38:00,718
I told you not to hurt her, but what?

594
00:38:00,718 --> 00:38:03,220
You embarrassed her in front of everyone!

595
00:38:04,088 --> 00:38:07,091
She's important to all of us,
and at the very least,

596
00:38:07,091 --> 00:38:10,094
she has done nothing but become nice to us!

597
00:38:13,831 --> 00:38:15,867
We bullied her from the start,

598
00:38:15,867 --> 00:38:18,736
but what you did is different.

599
00:38:18,736 --> 00:38:21,539
Give us one good reason why you did that.

600
00:38:21,539 --> 00:38:25,876
Because if you can't,
I am ashamed of you as a Ferell.

601
00:38:27,425 --> 00:38:29,714
Relax...

602
00:38:29,714 --> 00:38:32,250
It's your fault.

603
00:38:32,250 --> 00:38:34,351
Why did you do that?

604
00:38:35,286 --> 00:38:38,067
We were clear from the start...

605
00:38:38,067 --> 00:38:40,569
that we were just pretending.

606
00:38:41,559 --> 00:38:44,162
And now that
Antonia and I have gotten back together,

607
00:38:44,162 --> 00:38:46,063
I don't need her anymore.

608
00:38:47,432 --> 00:38:49,400
You're worthless, bro.

609
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:52,070
You're freaking worthless.

610
00:38:52,070 --> 00:38:54,638
You're annoying, bro.

611
00:39:05,149 --> 00:39:06,684
Babycakes...

612
00:39:06,684 --> 00:39:10,788
You know,
Florence's cooking was a bit salty earlier.

613
00:39:10,788 --> 00:39:13,591
It seems like it lacks the sweetness...

614
00:39:13,591 --> 00:39:17,394
of your love.

615
00:39:19,063 --> 00:39:21,032
You're something else.

616
00:39:21,032 --> 00:39:23,701
You might end up having diabetes

617
00:39:23,701 --> 00:39:25,403
because of too much love from me.

618
00:39:25,403 --> 00:39:27,071
My goodness!

619
00:39:27,071 --> 00:39:28,439
Type 1...

620
00:39:28,439 --> 00:39:30,341
Type 2 Diabetes...

621
00:39:30,341 --> 00:39:32,877
I don't care.

622
00:39:32,877 --> 00:39:38,750
Because what's important is, you're my type.

623
00:39:38,750 --> 00:39:40,684
Stop it.

624
00:39:43,187 --> 00:39:47,091
- Baby, you're something else.
- Ouch, that hurts.

625
00:39:47,091 --> 00:39:48,726
Don Ferell.

626
00:39:48,726 --> 00:39:50,962
It's you... again.

627
00:39:50,962 --> 00:39:53,031
Is there anything we can do for you, Sir?

628
00:39:53,031 --> 00:39:57,167
I want to know what's happening
in this house.

629
00:39:59,637 --> 00:40:02,686
We love each other, Don Ferell.

630
00:40:02,686 --> 00:40:07,779
Sir, I know
that workplace romances are frowned upon

631
00:40:07,779 --> 00:40:14,085
but I hope you'll understand
that we can't control our feelings.

632
00:40:14,085 --> 00:40:17,388
I'm not interested about the two of you.

633
00:40:17,388 --> 00:40:18,823
I've known about that for a long time now.

634
00:40:18,823 --> 00:40:19,957
Really?

635
00:40:19,957 --> 00:40:22,193
What do you want to know?

636
00:40:22,193 --> 00:40:27,265
Clearly, something is going on
between Florence and my grandsons.

637
00:40:27,265 --> 00:40:28,333
I want to find out.

638
00:40:28,333 --> 00:40:30,868
I want to know what's happening.

639
00:40:30,868 --> 00:40:33,163
Well, I agree with you, Sir,

640
00:40:33,163 --> 00:40:36,407
because I've noticed
something new happening to the kids.

641
00:40:36,407 --> 00:40:38,776
But there's only one way to find out,

642
00:40:38,776 --> 00:40:42,212
because the truth will set you free.

643
00:40:48,353 --> 00:40:51,301
Grandfather? What's this for?

644
00:40:51,301 --> 00:40:56,183
This is your chance to tell the truth,
or else,

645
00:40:56,183 --> 00:40:59,430
you know we know
where you feel ticklish the most.

646
00:40:59,430 --> 00:41:03,401
Nero is just using Florence
to get to Antonia.

647
00:41:03,401 --> 00:41:05,703
That's too painful.

648
00:41:05,703 --> 00:41:08,673
So you can imagine how Florence feels.

649
00:41:08,673 --> 00:41:12,441
I'm okay, but of course, I'm a bit...

650
00:41:12,441 --> 00:41:15,304
annoyed with what happened.

651
00:41:15,304 --> 00:41:16,681
But what can I do?

652
00:41:16,681 --> 00:41:20,351
I'm just a plain Dela Cruz, right?

653
00:41:20,351 --> 00:41:26,873
And the reason why I entered GU
is to study and achieve my dreams.

654
00:41:26,873 --> 00:41:28,112
What's your plan?

655
00:41:28,112 --> 00:41:31,182
I'm the only one who truly loves you, Nero.

656
00:41:31,182 --> 00:41:33,685
I'm the only person who can understand you.

657
00:41:33,685 --> 00:41:36,654
I will always protect you,
and I will never break your heart.

658
00:41:36,654 --> 00:41:38,456
What are you talking about?

659
00:41:38,456 --> 00:41:39,624
Break up with her.

660
00:41:39,624 --> 00:41:41,526
Do you think I want to reconcile with you?

661
00:41:41,526 --> 00:41:43,528
Do you think that you have a choice, Nero?

662
00:41:43,528 --> 00:41:45,196
I will make sure...

663
00:41:45,196 --> 00:41:48,333
that Florence will not just
be kicked out of university.

664
00:41:48,333 --> 00:41:51,269
Florence is an easy target.

665
00:41:51,269 --> 00:41:55,273
And I can hurt her in ways
that you can't even imagine.

666
00:41:55,273 --> 00:41:56,741
Nero is not here.

667
00:41:56,741 --> 00:41:59,243
Where did that kid go?
